{
  "amendment_2026-08-27": "Frozen contract amended AFTER the initial hash freeze but BEFORE any promotion: (1) harness/atomics_probe.m --init parsing used strtoull (big-endian numeric read) while casematrix.py stored init values as little-endian byte-hex strings (the same convention as every other *_hex field); this silently substituted the wrong bit pattern for da_smin/da_smax/da_exch*/da_store on the FIRST pair of capture runs, caught by analysis.py FAIL verdicts (never promoted, never cited). Fixed by parsing --init as LE-byte-hex like every other field (parse_le_hex()); the flawed first pair of runs was discarded before promotion (not renamed/retained -- no claim ever depended on them) and the matrix recaptured from scratch under the SAME run-ids after the fix. (2) casematrix.py case_order_sensitive_keys() excluded target_final_hex for tg_exch/tg_cmpxchg, but those shapes report their final value in tg_result_hex, not target_final_hex (a dev_*-only field) -- fixed to exclude tg_result_hex instead. (3) analysis.py check_ordering_probe substring-matched the wrong quote style against the real clang diagnostic. All three fixes are mechanical/objectively-forced (no discretion over the correct fix) and are recorded in PROGRESS.md with the full diagnostic evidence. The two promoted runs (run01, run02) were captured AFTER every fix, from byte-identical authored source (00_inputs.json authored_sha256 matches exactly).",
